{"source_type":"article","title":"Aramaic Incantation Texts between Orality and Textuality","authors":"Charles G. Häberl","issued_year":2015,"citation":"Häberl, Charles G. 'Aramaic Incantation Texts between Orality and Textuality.' 2015.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"The oral-performance side of the orality/writtenness dispute the review records in §7, against Waller's written-performativity position. Container details need establishing."}
{"source_type":"article","title":"Hebrew in the Incantation Bowls","authors":"Daniel Frim","issued_year":2021,"container_title":"Journal of Semitic Studies","citation":"Frim, Daniel. 'Hebrew in the Incantation Bowls.' Journal of Semitic Studies 66 (2021): 27–51.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"With Molin, establishes the bowls as the only epigraphic witnesses to Biblical Hebrew from late antique Babylonia."}
{"source_type":"article","title":"Babylonian Talmud, Bowls, and Jewish Textuality","authors":"Shai Secunda","issued_year":2025,"container_title":"Jewish Quarterly Review","citation":"Secunda, Shai. 'Babylonian Talmud, Bowls, and Jewish Textuality.' Jewish Quarterly Review 115 (2025): 413–451.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"Treats Talmud and bowls as participants in one Babylonian textual culture, emphasising reworking and circulation over exact quotation."}
{"source_type":"article","title":"An Unpublished Syriac Bowl (B9002) with a Mandaic Incantation","authors":"Simcha Gross; Michele Scarlassara","issued_year":2025,"container_title":"Aramaic Studies","doi":"10.1163/17455227-bja10059","url":"https://doi.org/10.1163/17455227-bja10059","citation":"Gross, Simcha, and Michele Scarlassara. 'An Unpublished Syriac Bowl (B9002) with a Mandaic Incantation.' Aramaic Studies 23 (2025): 22–54. DOI: 10.1163/17455227-bja10059.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"Multispectral imaging reveals a near-verbatim Mandaic incantation in a Syriac-script bowl: cross-script transmission as an object-level fact rather than a general theory. B9002 is a specific object to look for in the corpus."}
{"source_type":"article","title":"Exploring the 'Cozy Cabal of Academics, Dealers and Collectors' through the Schøyen Collection","authors":"Simon Mackenzie; and colleagues","issued_year":2020,"container_title":"Heritage","citation":"Mackenzie, Simon, and colleagues. 'Exploring the \"Cozy Cabal of Academics, Dealers and Collectors\" through the Schøyen Collection.' Heritage 3 (2020).","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"unknown","notes":"Provenance and research-ethics literature on the Schøyen bowls, alongside Brodie 2014 and 2023. Full author list, volume and pages need establishing."}
{"source_type":"article","title":"Jewish Legal Formulae in the Aramaic Incantation Bowls","authors":"Avigail Manekin-Bamberger","issued_year":2015,"container_title":"Aramaic Studies","citation":"Manekin-Bamberger, Avigail. 'Jewish Legal Formulae in the Aramaic Incantation Bowls.' Aramaic Studies 13 (2015): 69–81.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"Divorce, oath, vow and excommunication language repurposed as supernatural acts. The review is explicit that technical resemblance shows familiarity with authoritative legal forms and does not prove a rabbinic court produced the bowl."}
