{"source_type":"article","title":"Magic Formulae and Women's History","authors":"Avigail Manekin-Bamberger","issued_year":2025,"container_title":"Jewish Quarterly Review","doi":"10.1353/jqr.2025.a952518","url":"https://doi.org/10.1353/jqr.2025.a952518","citation":"Manekin-Bamberger, Avigail. 'Magic Formulae and Women's History.' Jewish Quarterly Review 115 (2025): 1–32. DOI: 10.1353/jqr.2025.a952518.","access_status":"unknown","rights_status":"copyrighted","notes":"Challenges direct female-authorship inference from formulaic first-person texts. Read against Kedar 2019, whose authorship attributions the index already stores as `handwriting_attribution` claims."}
